' S-609 (2026-10-17): legacy AST-x64 did not know the result type of `Say.Selam("x")` (a STATIC method named through its class) and PRINT
' wrote the returned STRING pointer as a number. WASM cannot print strings (explicit rejection), so five engines run this.
CLASS Say
    PUBLIC
    STATIC METHOD Selam(ad AS STRING) AS STRING
        RETURN "Merhaba " + ad
    END METHOD
END CLASS
PRINT Say.Selam("Ayse")
